    "# Phase 8: Drift Detection & Adaptive Retraining Pipeline\n",
    "## Project: Adaptive Learning for Cloud Security and Predictive Maintenance\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective:\n",
    "Simulate a shifting cloud network environment, detect statistical distribution drift using the **Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) Test**, execute adaptive model retraining, and conditionally deploy the updated model only if validation performance improves."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure path to src is available\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))) if '__file__' in locals() else os.path.abspath('..')\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, 'src', 'adaptive'))\n",
    "\n",
    "from retrain import run_adaptive_pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Adaptive module imported successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 1. Environment B Shift & KS Drift Detection Method\n",
    "\n",
    "### A. Environment B Simulation Logic:\n",
    "1. **Concept / Class Ratio Shift**: Attack traffic is resampled to **75% of total instances** (up from 45% in baseline training), simulating a sudden cyber-attack burst or Distributed Denial of Service (DoS) storm.\n",
    "2. **Covariate Feature Shift**: Key continuous traffic features (`dur`, `sbytes`, `dbytes`, `rate`, `sttl`) are modified with mean/std noise ($\mu=+1.2, \sigma=0.4$) to simulate altered network routing or changed payload behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "### B. Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) Test:\n",
    "- The 2-sample KS test measures the maximum distance between cumulative distribution functions (CDFs) of Environment A ($F_A(x)$) and Environment B ($F_B(x)$):\n",
    "$$D = \\sup_x |F_A(x) - F_B(x)|$$\n",
    "- Feature drift is flagged if $p\\text{-value} < 0.05$ AND $D > 0.15$. System-wide drift is flagged if $\\ge 15\\%$ of features exhibit statistical drift."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 2. Execute Adaptive Retraining Pipeline"
   ]
